    "summary" : "The coding discipline: build, run, test and save a project through the editor's own commands. An application joins this discipline by realizing one of these Skills — which is what gives its place the coding focus. READING AND EDITING CODE ARE NOT HERE, and their absence is deliberate: a Skill that returns a value needs a compiled provider, and Mary has no code-surface adapter yet (the prose-surface lane's analogue for code). Every Skill below is a chord the managed-UI engine can actually press.",
